## Actual R7 examples and source

The immutable `supporting-evidence/visuals/r7-replay/` folder contains the reviewed actual shared components. Open index.html through an existing local static server; no new framework or installation is needed. Its embedded intake counts are historical; use current-authority for requirements. The fallback package keeps the exact source/build manifests. The copied reviewed/current-main code and their diff supply concrete component-level examples; they are evidence to reconcile, not permission to merge the whole preview branch.

- Dialog focus: `scene.html?view=timed&state=ladder&stage=capped&rounds=12&hold=1&backdrop=balanced&overlay=dialog&skin=signal` and rounds=4. Current continuous frame/selected style is visible; P01–P03 remain final corrections.
- Live ladder: `scene.html?view=timed&state=ladder&rounds=4&overlay=dialog&skin=signal`; Start, check through a rung, Finish, then Undo. Preserve checked progress and draft/original cap; apply P04 text inset.
- Shared logging: index Section 3 includes all 16 named moments and actual forms; review-cases.json pins each query. Use this inventory across app consumers rather than verifying only one lift.
- Compact equipment: `scene.html?view=timed&state=emom&equipment=name&overlay=dialog&skin=signal`; also state=for_time/AMRAP for medicine-ball/bodyweight context. Section 4 selected A governs old dedicated equipment lines.
- Soft aura: `scene.html?view=timed&state=emom&stage=five&hold=1&overlay=dialog&skin=signal`. The 70px / 1.5s smooth aura is confirmed. P05 adds matching timer phase/rhythm. Test stage=ten, count-up cap, pause/expiry, reduce=1 and rest inside an open native dialog too.
- Final five expected changes: P01–P05 in FINAL-POLISH-ACCEPTANCE.md are explicit geometry/behavior contracts. They are not depicted as already-implemented screenshots. Capture real before/after implementation evidence during build, keeping frame/viewport and entry state comparable.

## Delivery evidence that cannot be skipped

For each user-facing criterion, record entry route/state and action, expected resulting UI/data/recovery, named integration owner, exact delivered source revision and concrete artifact reference. Use current runtime screenshots for static layout, computed geometry for alignment/frames/gaps, a short motion clip or timed samples for synchronized pulse, and real schema/write/read/reload proof for persistence. Include relevant error/retry/focus/reduced-motion and skin/viewport cases. A helper exists in a gallery is not proof that an application route consumes it; a synthetic save is not backend proof. Every final route journey needs a completion owner and named verification in plan-v5.

